# pyenv
#   For a library or package, you might want to ignore these files since the code is
#   intended to run an multiple environments; otherwise, check them in:
# .python-version

# pipenv
#   According to pypa/pipenv#598, it is recommended to include Pipfile.lock in version control.
#   However, in some cases, pipenv users prefer to skip Pipfile.lock, when creating a library.
#   Pipfile.lock

# poetry
#   Similar to Pipfile.lock, it is generally recommended to include poetry.lock in version control.
#   This is especially recommended for binary packages to ensure reproducible builds.
# poetry.lock

# pdm
#   Similar to Pipfile.lock, it is generally recommended to include pdm.lock in version control.
# pdm.lock

# PEP 582; used by e.g. github.com/davidhalter/jedi-vim, github.com/pdm-project/pdm
